    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2C1Tfw69DcoEtS6XhVSXRCT)_\n\n## Merge order\n\n- Independent of other open PRs; it builds on merged #489 (lint keys), #474 and #475.\n- Touches `sp-keys` (4 lines in `L b f`), `sp-academic` (one `require`) and `sp-backup-lookup` (one list entry). A conflict in those files is trivial.\n\n## Summary\n\n- New module `sp-bibtex-abstract` (literate doc: `docs/tangles/academic/sp-bibtex-abstract.org`).\n- Moves the `abstract` field of a BibTeX entry into its litnote under `* Abstract`.\n- Keys under `C-; L b f`:\n  - `B` dry-run report (Org table sections, `d`/`u`/`A`/`g` as in the other lints)\n  - `b` move the abstracts of a whole file, after one question, in batches\n  - `e` move the abstract of the entry at point (prefix: dry run)\n  - `R` restore a run from its backup\n- Safety:\n  - Note first: saved, then read back from disk; only if it holds the abstract does the field leave the `.bib`.\n  - The `.bib` is written once, at the end, with verified entries only; every other field of an entry must be unchanged or the entry is left alone.\n  - Note writes only add (`sp-litnotes-meta--verify-kept`).\n- Matching and edge cases:\n  - Entry-to-note matching uses `sp-author-notes-bibtex--covered` (ROAM_REFS / `#+reference:`).\n  - `* Abstract` missing: created as the first heading. Empty: filled. Same text: only the field goes.\n  - Different text: conflict, reported with both texts, nothing overwritten.\n  - No litnote: skipped and listed. Macro, concatenation or empty abstract: listed as a problem.\n- Conversion: abstract is converted to Org (accents to Unicode, `\\emph` to `/x/`, `\\&` etc., braces removed, `$math$` kept verbatim, unknown commands kept and named in the report).\n- Backup: `sp-bibtex-abstract-backup-directory/<stamp>/` holds the `.bib`, changed notes and a manifest; also visible to `sp-backup-lookup`.\n- Tests: `tests/sp-bibtex-abstract-test.el` (23, Emacs 29 batch, temp files) plus a keys test; the lint, meta and keys suites still pass. Not run on the real vault.\n- Not changed: no CHANGELOG edit; the main `sp-bibtex-lint-dryrun` report has no abstract button yet.\n\n## Manual testing\n\n- [ ] Pull this branch, restart Emacs (or `M-x sp-reload-modules`)\n- [ ] Copy a few entries with abstracts into a scratch `.bib` that is in `sp-bibtex-files` (untested by Claude on the real vault)\n- [ ] `C-; L b f B` on it: report lists movable, conflicts, no-litnote and problems; nothing on disk changes\n- [ ] In a `.bib` buffer, `C-u C-; L b f e` on one entry: message only\n- [ ] `C-; L b f e` on one entry: confirm; note gets `* Abstract` as its first heading, field is gone from the buffer (unsaved), `C-/` brings it back\n- [ ] Edge: entry whose note already has a different `* Abstract`: refused, nothing changes\n- [ ] Edge: entry without a litnote and one with a LaTeX-heavy abstract (accents, `\\emph`, `$x$`): skipped / converted as described\n- [ ] `C-; L b f b` on the scratch file: one question, backup folder reported, fields removed, notes have the text\n- [ ] Open a moved note: heading, text and meta lines look right; `vulpea` finds it\n- [ ] Run `C-; L b f b` again: \"No abstract to move\"\n- [ ] `C-; L b f R`: `.bib` and notes are back as before the run\n- [ ] Regression: `C-; L b l` and `C-; L b f c` still work\n\n<details><summary>Revert after testing</summary>\n\n- Discard local edits made while testing: `git -C ~/dotfiles status`, then `git -C ~/dotfiles restore .` (`git clean -fd` only after `git clean -nd`).\n- Return to main: `git -C ~/dotfiles switch main` and `git -C ~/dotfiles pull`.\n- Optionally delete the test branch locally: `git -C ~/dotfiles branch -D claude/project-thread-jtrror`.\n- Restart Emacs (or `M-x sp-reload-modules`).\n- If the vault changed, use `C-; L b f R`, or restore from `sp-bibtex-abstract-backup-directory/<stamp>/`.\n\n</details>\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNi9pYp9dtCTs91ttKJG)_",
